# Figure 8 - Omega (spin-orbit) potential energy curves of RaSe
# Londono & Perez-Rios, "Electronic properties of the Radium-monochalcogenides
# RaX (X = O,S,Se) and RaO+/- ions"
#
# Method : MCSCF / MRCI+Q + ECP78MDF (Ra) + ECP10MDF / aug-cc-pV5Z-PP (Se), with
#          the one- and two-electron Pauli-Breit operator diagonalised over the
#          lowest Lambda-S states.
# Source : author's own MRCI+SO output, SO/*_orig.txt (absolute hartree).
#          Converted with 1 Eh = 219474.6313702 cm^-1 and referenced to the
#          X1Sigma+_0+ minimum on the grid, E0 = -395.76700228 Eh, so the
#          absolute energies are recoverable as E(Eh) = E0 + col/219474.6313702.
#
# THIS IS THE AB INITIO GRID (17 points, R = 2.60 - 3.95 A).  A 500-point
# version exists in SO/Norm/; it is a cubic spline through these points
# (reproduces them to 1e-4 cm^-1) and is not archived.  Note that the 500-point
# files start at R = 2.59 A, so their first four points are spline
# EXTRAPOLATION below the computed range, not data.
#
# Columns
#   1  R              internuclear separation   [Angstrom]
#   2  X1Sigma+_0+    [cm^-1]
#   3  a3Pi_0+        [cm^-1]
#   4  a3Pi_0-        [cm^-1]   -- reliable only for 2.75 <= R <= 3.40, see below
#   5  a3Pi_1         [cm^-1]
#   6  a3Pi_2         [cm^-1]
#   7  A1Pi_1         [cm^-1]
#
# There is no B1Sigma+_0+ column: RaSe has no such file and no such row in
# Table VII, the Lambda-S B1Sigma+ lying at 24039 cm^-1 (Table V), far above
# this manifold.  RaO resolves seven Omega states, RaSe six.
#
# Spectroscopic constants: parabola fitted over +/-0.06 A about the minimum of
# the cubic spline of the points below, reproducible from this file alone.
# mu(226Ra-80Se) = 59.04114 amu.
#   state          Re(A)  Re pub |   Te(cm-1)   Te pub |  we(cm-1)  we pub
#   X1Sigma+_0+    2.759   2.764 |     -10.31      0.00 |     248.0   247.3
#   a3Pi_0+        3.129   3.128 |    6558.37   6567.58 |     147.2   147.1
#   a3Pi_0-        3.129       - |    6558.27       - |     146.8       -
#   a3Pi_1         3.126   3.125 |    8011.81   8021.02 |     145.3   145.3
#   a3Pi_2         3.127   3.126 |    7852.75   7861.96 |     144.9   144.9
#   A1Pi_1         3.128   3.127 |    6690.99   6700.21 |     147.2   147.2
#
#   Every excited-state Te above sits 9.21 cm^-1 below its Table VII value, to
#   within 0.01 cm^-1 across all four states.  That is a pure zero-point offset
#   - Table VII located the X1Sigma+_0+ minimum slightly differently - not a
#   disagreement about the curves: the state-to-state spacings agree to better
#   than 0.1 cm^-1, as do Re (<= 0.005 A) and we (<= 0.7 cm^-1).
#
# ROOT-TRACKING PROBLEM IN a3Pi_0- (column 4) - please check before archiving.
#   The 0- component of a 3Pi state should stay nearly degenerate with its 0+
#   partner.  Over 2.75 <= R <= 3.40 A it does: the two agree to 0.3-1.9 cm^-1,
#   which is the expected behaviour.  Outside that window column 4 tracks a
#   different state entirely:
#
#     R (A)     |0- minus 0+|   |0- minus X1Sigma+_0+|   |0- minus A1Pi_1|
#      2.60         1537.7                 12909.4                9.0
#      2.65          780.9                 12436.3               12.5
#      2.70           48.4                 11722.6                5.4
#      2.75            1.9                 10460.9              133.7   <- ok
#      2.80            1.8                  9211.3              134.9   <- ok
#      2.85            0.3                  8111.8              134.1   <- ok
#      2.90            0.4                  7084.2              132.5   <- ok
#      2.95            0.5                  6114.5              131.6   <- ok
#      3.00            0.6                  5204.9              131.2   <- ok
#      3.10            0.8                  3699.1              132.1   <- ok
#      3.20            1.1                  2276.7              134.8   <- ok
#      3.30            1.4                  1145.1              138.8   <- ok
#      3.40            1.8                   301.9              143.8   <- ok
#      3.50          263.6                     2.3              149.7
#      3.60          593.9                     3.0              156.3
#      3.75          835.5                     3.8              166.7
#      3.95          960.9                     5.1              181.8
#
#   For R <= 2.70 A column 4 sits within 5-13 cm^-1 of A1Pi_1, and for
#   R >= 3.50 A within 2-5 cm^-1 of X1Sigma+_0+.  Omega = 0-, 0+ and 1 are
#   different symmetry species: they may cross at a point, but nothing couples
#   them, so tracking one another over several consecutive geometries is a
#   labelling problem, not physics.  The values are left in place because they
#   are genuine eigenvalues of the Pauli-Breit matrix - only the assignment to
#   a3Pi_0- is in doubt outside 2.75-3.40 A.
#
# Extracted 2026-09-25
#
